row(21, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'ARAD HEARD — BY THE WAY OF ATHARIM, THE SPIES\' ROAD IN THE TRANSLATION. "{H(21, 1, "וישמע", "הכנעני", "מלך", "ערד", "ישב", "הנגב")}" ("and the Canaanite king of Arad, who dwelt in the south, heard" — the clause at this seat and at the itinerary\'s 33:40, where it stands AFTER Aaron\'s death as here; Arad\'s five seats — Judah and Simeon\'s Zephath in the Negev of Arad (Judg 1:16-17), two kings, Hormah\'s and Arad\'s (Josh 12:14); computed) → {A(21, 1, "ושמע", "כנענאה", "מלכא", "דערד", "יתב", "דרומא")} ("and the Canaanite king of Arad, who dwelt in the south, heard"); "{H(21, 1, "כי", "בא", "ישראל", "דרך", "האתרים")}" ("that Israel came by the way of ATHARIM" — a hapax) → {A(21, 1, "ארי", "אתא", "ישראל", "ארח", "מאלליא")} ("that Israel came by the way of THE SPIES" — the translation reads the place-name as the spies\' road, with the Aramaic root it gives 13:2\'s "to spy out" and 21:32\'s "to spy", cut from the shelf\'s bytes); "{H(21, 1, "וילחם", "בישראל", "וישב", "ממנו", "שבי")}" ("and he fought against Israel and took from them a captivity" — one seat) → {A(21, 1, "ואגח", "קרבא", "בישראל", "ושבא", "מניה", "שביא")} ("and he waged war against Israel and took from them a captivity"). The register: "and he heard", "and he fought", "and he took captive".')
row(21, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'ISRAEL VOWED A VOW — JACOB\'S FORMULA; IF YOU WILL SURELY GIVE; I WILL DEVOTE. "{H(21, 2, "וידר", "ישראל", "נדר", "ליהוה")}" ("and Israel vowed a vow to the LORD" — "vowed a vow" with the subject between: JACOB at Bethel (Gen 28:20), ISRAEL here — the one man\'s two names on the Torah\'s two vows — and Jephthah\'s (Judg 11:30) the run; computed) → {A(21, 2, "וקים", "ישראל", "קים", "קדם", "יי")} ("and Israel ESTABLISHED A COVENANT before the LORD" — the vow rendered a kiyam, cut from the shelf\'s bytes); "{H(21, 2, "אם", "נתן", "תתן", "את", "העם", "הזה", "בידי")}" ("if You will surely give this people into my hand" — the doubled infinitive\'s one seat) → {A(21, 2, "אם", "ממסר", "תמסר", "ית", "עמא", "הדין", "בידי")} ("if You will surely deliver this people into my hand" — the doubling kept); "{H(21, 2, "והחרמתי", "את", "עריהם")}" ("then I will DEVOTE their cities" — the verb here and Micah 4:13; the war-cherem of Lev 27:28-29 and Deut 7:2, 13:16, 20:17; 18:14\'s "every devoted thing" the priests\' — the same root; computed) → {A(21, 2, "ואגמר", "ית", "קרויהון")} ("then I will DESTROY their cities" — the devotion a destruction). The register: "and he vowed", "and he said".')
row(21, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'HORMAH NAMED — SIX CHAPTERS AFTER ITS USE. "{H(21, 3, "וישמע", "יהוה", "בקול", "ישראל", "ויתן", "את", "הכנעני")}" ("and the LORD heard the voice of Israel and gave up the Canaanite" — "heard the voice of Israel" one seat) → {A(21, 3, "וקביל", "יי", "צלותיה", "דישראל", "ומסר", "ית", "כנענאה")} ("and the LORD ACCEPTED THE PRAYER of Israel and delivered the Canaanite" — the voice made a prayer, cut from the shelf\'s bytes); "{H(21, 3, "ויחרם", "אתהם", "ואת", "עריהם")}" ("and he devoted them and their cities") → {A(21, 3, "וגמר", "יתהון", "וית", "קרויהון")} ("and he destroyed them and their cities"); "{H(21, 3, "ויקרא", "שם", "המקום", "חרמה")}" ("and he called the name of the place HORMAH" — the naming at 21:3 of the name the ink USED at 14:45 (the spies\' rout "as far as Hormah" — sitting 4\'s find; the registry row carries both verses); Judah names it AGAIN, "the name of the city Hormah" (Judg 1:17); Hormah\'s eight seats; "and he called the name of the place" the formula of MASSAH-AND-MERIBAH (Exod 17:7), Peniel, Taberah, Gilgal; computed) → {A(21, 3, "וקרא", "שמא", "דאתרא", "חרמה")} ("and he called the name of the place Hormah"). The register: "and He heard", "and He gave", "and he devoted", "and he called".')
row(21, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'FROM MOUNT HOR BY THE RED SEA ROAD — THE COMMAND OF 14:25 RUN; THE SOUL SHORTENED. "{H(21, 4, "ויסעו", "מהר", "ההר", "דרך", "ים", "סוף", "לסבב", "את", "ארץ", "אדום")}" ("and they journeyed from Mount Hor by the way of the Red Sea, to go around the land of Edom" — "by the way of the Red Sea" at four seats: THE DECREE\'S COMMAND "turn and journey into the wilderness by the way of the Red Sea" (14:25 — sitting 4b\'s open debit, its RUN here), this, and Deuteronomy\'s two retellings (1:40, 2:1); "to go around the land of Edom" one seat — Edom\'s refusal (20:21) run; computed) → {A(21, 4, "ונטלו", "מהר", "טורא", "ארח", "ימא", "דסוף", "לאקפא", "ית", "ארעא", "דאדום")} ("and they journeyed from Hor the mountain by the way of the Reed Sea, to go around the land of Edom"); "{H(21, 4, "ותקצר", "נפש", "העם", "בדרך")}" ("and the soul of the people was SHORTENED on the way" — the idiom\'s four seats: Israel\'s at Gilead\'s misery (Judg 10:16), SAMSON\'S at Delilah\'s nagging (16:16), this, Zechariah\'s; 11:23\'s "is the LORD\'s hand short" the verb\'s other Torah seat, Deut 24:19\'s "when you REAP" its consonantal homograph; computed) → {A(21, 4, "ועקת", "נפשא", "דעמא", "באורחא")} ("and the soul of the people was DISTRESSED on the way"). The register: "and they journeyed", "and it was shortened".')
row(21, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'THE PEOPLE SPOKE AGAINST GOD AND MOSES — THE SEA\'S COMPLAINT, THE ROTTEN BREAD. "{H(21, 5, "וידבר", "העם", "באלהים", "ובמשה")}" ("and the people spoke against God and against Moses" — one seat; Psalm 78:19 "they spoke against God" the retelling\'s verb) → {A(21, 5, "ואתרעם", "עמא", "במימרא", "דיי", "ועם", "משה", "נצו")} ("and the people MURMURED against the WORD of the LORD, and with Moses they STROVE" — two verbs for one, the Memra inserted, cut from the shelf\'s bytes); "{H(21, 5, "למה", "העליתנו", "ממצרים", "למות", "במדבר")}" ("why did you bring us up from Egypt to die in the wilderness" — the first Meribah\'s clause (Exod 17:3) a third time, after 20:5; "to die in the wilderness" THE SEA\'S complaint (Exod 14:11) and this; computed) → {A(21, 5, "למא", "אסקתונא", "ממצרים", "לממת", "במדברא")} ("why did you bring us up from Egypt to die in the wilderness"); "{H(21, 5, "כי", "אין", "לחם", "ואין", "מים")}" ("for there is no bread and no water" — one seat) → {A(21, 5, "ארי", "לית", "לחמא", "ולית", "מיא")} ("for there is no bread and no water"); "{H(21, 5, "ונפשנו", "קצה", "בלחם", "הקלקל")}" ("and our soul loathes the LIGHT bread" — "the light bread" a hapax; the loathe-verb Rebekah\'s "I loathe my life" (Gen 27:46), the land\'s (Lev 20:23) and this; computed) → {A(21, 5, "ונפשנא", "עקת", "במנא", "הדין", "דמיכליה", "קליל")} ("and our soul is distressed with THIS MANNA whose food is light" — THE TRANSLATION NAMES THE MANNA the ink leaves unnamed, cut from the shelf\'s bytes). The register: "and he spoke".')
row(21, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'THE FIERY SERPENTS — THE BURN-WORD; THEY BIT — USURY\'S VERB. "{H(21, 6, "וישלח", "יהוה", "בעם", "את", "הנחשים", "השרפים")}" ("and the LORD sent among the people the FIERY serpents" — one seat; the saraph-word\'s consonants are 19:5\'s "he shall BURN the heifer", 17:4\'s "the BURNT ones", Isaiah\'s seraphim (6:2, 6:6); Deut 8:15\'s "fiery serpent and scorpion" the retelling; computed) → {A(21, 6, "וגרי", "יי", "בעמא", "ית", "חיון", "קלן")} ("and the LORD INCITED among the people the BURNING serpents"); "{H(21, 6, "וינשכו", "את", "העם", "וימת", "עם", "רב", "מישראל")}" ("and they BIT the people, and many people of Israel died" — THE BITE-VERB: Dan\'s serpent "that bites the horse\'s heels" (Gen 49:17), the serpents\' three (21:6, 8, 9), and USURY\'S bite — "you shall not lend at BITE" (Exod 22:24, Lev 25:36-37, Deut 23:20-21), Proverbs\' wine "bites like a serpent"; one root; computed) → {A(21, 6, "ונכיתו", "ית", "עמא", "ומית", "עם", "סגי", "מישראל")} ("and they bit the people, and many people of Israel died"). The register: "and He sent", "and they bit", "and he died".')
row(21, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'WE HAVE SINNED; PRAY — THE BIBLE\'S FIRST PRAYER-VERB; THE SERPENT, SINGULAR. "{H(21, 7, "ויבא", "העם", "אל", "משה", "ויאמרו", "חטאנו", "כי", "דברנו", "ביהוה", "ובך")}" ("and the people came to Moses and said: we have sinned, for we spoke against the LORD and against you" — "we have sinned, for we spoke" one seat) → {A(21, 7, "ואתא", "עמא", "למשה", "ואמרו", "חבנא", "ארי", "אתרעמנא", "קדם", "יי", "ועמך", "נצינא")} ("we have sinned, for we MURMURED before the LORD and STROVE with you" — the two verbs again); "{H(21, 7, "התפלל", "אל", "יהוה", "ויסר", "מעלינו", "את", "הנחש")}" ("PRAY to the LORD that He remove from us THE SERPENT" — the pray-verb whose first seat is Abraham\'s for Abimelech, "he is a prophet and he will PRAY for you" (Gen 20:7); "remove from us" one seat; THE SERPENT SINGULAR where 21:6 sent "the serpents" — computed) → {A(21, 7, "צלי", "קדם", "יי", "ויעדי", "מננא", "ית", "חויא")} ("pray before the LORD that He remove from us the serpent"); "{H(21, 7, "ויתפלל", "משה", "בעד", "העם")}" ("and Moses prayed for the people" — "and Moses prayed" at TWO seats, Taberah\'s fire (11:2) and this; computed) → {A(21, 7, "וצלי", "משה", "על", "עמא")} ("and Moses prayed for the people"). The register: "and he came", "and they said", "and he prayed".')
row(21, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'MAKE A SERAPH, SET IT ON A POLE — THE POLE-WORD OF YHWH-NISSI AND KORACH\'S SIGN. "{H(21, 8, "ויאמר", "יהוה", "אל", "משה", "עשה", "לך", "שרף")}" ("and the LORD said to Moses: make yourself a SERAPH" — one seat; the frame to Moses alone) → {A(21, 8, "ואמר", "יי", "למשה", "עביד", "לך", "קליא")} ("and the LORD said to Moses: make yourself a BURNING ONE"); "{H(21, 8, "ושים", "אתו", "על", "נס")}" ("and set it on a POLE" — THE POLE-WORD (nes, the tsere) in the Torah at four seats: Moses\' altar-name after the first Meribah, "YHWH is my banner" (Exod 17:15), the serpent\'s pole (21:8-9) and KORACH\'S two hundred and fifty who "became a SIGN" (26:10); "fled" (Deut 34:7) and "to flee" (the manslayer\'s, 35:6) its consonantal homographs, told by the points; computed) → {A(21, 8, "ושוי", "יתיה", "על", "את")} ("and set it on a SIGN" — the pole rendered by the sign-word the translation gives Korach\'s "sign" at 26:10: the serpent\'s pole and the censers\' warning one Aramaic word, cut from both seats\' bytes); "{H(21, 8, "והיה", "כל", "הנשוך", "וראה", "אתו", "וחי")}" ("and it shall be, everyone bitten who sees it shall LIVE" — one seat; the exam\'s Rosh Hashanah 3:8 "does the serpent kill or give life?" the compile\'s docket) → {A(21, 8, "ויהי", "כל", "דיתנכית", "ויחזי", "יתיה", "ויתקים")} ("and it shall be, everyone bitten who sees it shall be SUSTAINED"). The register: "and He said".')
row(21, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'A SERPENT OF COPPER — THE PUN THE ARAMAIC LOSES; THE LOOK THAT HEALS, LOT\'S WIFE\'S THAT KILLED; NEHUSHTAN. "{H(21, 9, "ויעש", "משה", "נחש", "נחשת", "וישמהו", "על", "הנס")}" ("and Moses made a serpent of COPPER and set it on the pole" — "a serpent of copper" here and at its END, 2 Kgs 18:4: Hezekiah "crushed the copper serpent that Moses had made, for until those days Israel burned incense to it, and called it NEHUSHTAN" — the object\'s whole career in the ink; the verse\'s five serpent-and-copper tokens one consonantal play; computed) → {A(21, 9, "ועבד", "משה", "חויא", "דנחשא", "ושוייה", "על", "את")} ("and Moses made a serpent of copper and set it on the sign" — THE PUN LOST: the Aramaic serpent is chivya, the copper nechasha, cut from the shelf\'s bytes); "{H(21, 9, "והיה", "אם", "נשך", "הנחש", "את", "איש", "והביט", "אל", "נחש", "הנחשת", "וחי")}" ("and it was, if the serpent bit a man, he LOOKED at the serpent of copper and lived" — THE LOOK-VERB\'S Torah seven: Abraham "look at the heavens" (Gen 15:5), LOT\'S WIFE "looked behind him and became a pillar of salt" (19:26) after "do not look behind you" (19:17), Moses "feared to look" (Exod 3:6), Moses beholds the LORD\'s likeness (12:8), this, Balaam\'s 23:21 — the look that killed at Sodom, the look that heals here; computed) → {A(21, 9, "והוה", "כד", "נכית", "חויא", "ית", "גברא", "ומסתכל", "לחויא", "דנחשא", "ומתקים")} ("and it was, when the serpent bit a man, he GAZED at the serpent of copper and was sustained"). The register: "and he made", "and he set it".')
