row(21, 34, 'MATERIAL', f'DO NOT FEAR HIM — THE ORACLE DEUTERONOMY REPEATS WITH ONE WORD CHANGED, AND JOSHUA INHERITS. "{H(21, 34, "ויאמר", "יהוה", "אל", "משה", "אל", "תירא", "אתו")}" ("and the LORD said to Moses: do not fear him" — "do not fear him" at TWO seats: this and Deuteronomy 3:2, which is THIS VERSE with ONE TOKEN changed, "to Moses" → "to me" — every other word shared, computed; the formula "do not fear... for into your hand I have given" is JOSHUA\'S at Ai (8:1) and Gibeon (10:8)) → {A(21, 34, "ואמר", "יי", "למשה", "לא", "תדחל", "מניה")} ("and the LORD said to Moses: do not fear him"); "{H(21, 34, "כי", "בידך", "נתתי", "אתו", "ואת", "כל", "עמו", "ואת", "ארצו")}" ("for into your hand I have given him and all his people and his land" — "for into your hand I have given" here and Deut 3:2) → {A(21, 34, "ארי", "בידך", "מסרית", "יתיה", "וית", "כל", "עמיה", "וית", "ארעיה")} ("for into your hand I have delivered him and all his people and his land"); "{H(21, 34, "ועשית", "לו", "כאשר", "עשית", "לסיחן", "מלך", "האמרי", "אשר", "יושב", "בחשבון")}" ("and you shall do to him as you did to Sihon king of the Amorite who dwelt in Heshbon" — the Sihon precedent cited inside the Og oracle; the pair Sihon-and-Og the Psalms\' refrain, 135:11, 136:19-20) → {A(21, 34, "ותעבד", "ליה", "כמא", "די", "עבדת", "לסיחון", "מלכא", "דאמוראה", "די", "יתב", "בחשבון")} ("and you shall do to him as you did to Sihon king of the Amorite who dwelt in Heshbon"). The register: "and He said".')
row(21, 35, 'MATERIAL', f'NO SURVIVOR LEFT — JOSHUA\'S REFRAIN BORN. "{H(21, 35, "ויכו", "אתו", "ואת", "בניו", "ואת", "כל", "עמו", "עד", "בלתי", "השאיר", "לו", "שריד")}" ("and they struck him and his sons and all his people, until no survivor was left to him" — "until no survivor was left to him" at five seats: Og\'s, Deuteronomy\'s retelling (3:3 — which DROPS "his sons"), JOSHUA\'S Ai (8:22) and Gezer (10:33), Jehu\'s (2 Kgs 10:11); the survivor-word the campaign\'s refrain at Joshua 10:28-40, 11:8 — the formula of the first conquest east of the Jordan carried into the conquest west; Og "of the remnant of the Rephaim", his iron bed nine cubits by four (Deut 3:11, the parser reads 9, 4); computed) → {A(21, 35, "ומחו", "יתיה", "וית", "בנוהי", "וית", "כל", "עמיה", "עד", "דלא", "אשתאר", "ליה", "משזיב")} ("and they struck him and his sons and all his people, until no ESCAPER was left to him"); "{H(21, 35, "ויירשו", "את", "ארצו")}" ("and they possessed his land" — with Deut 4:47; the portion ends in possession, its next verse (22:1, Balak\'s draft) the plains of Moab) → {A(21, 35, "ויריתו", "ית", "ארעיה")} ("and they inherited his land"). The register: "and they struck", "and they possessed".')
